    sample: { kicker: 'Chapter III', headline: 'Hand carved.', sub: 'Black ink, red ink, and a heavy press.' },
    guide: { signs: 'Cream paper; heavy black ink with carved, slightly rough edges; one second ink (red) printed a little out of register; pictures made of fine parallel cut lines; chunky slab capitals; things land with the thump of a press rather than sliding.', build: 'Pictures and footage get the "engrave" clip (ink the text colour, paper empty or the background, lines 70-110) so they read as cut lines. Shapes are flat black or red with a "paper" clip (rough 1-1.5, grain 0.2) for carved edges. Titles land with text-slam (no blur) and a stamp sound; a text-3d with depth 2 in the red ink under a black title gives the misregistered second plate. A slight boil at 4 fps on still frames for a printed jitter.' },
