    sample: { kicker: 'Round one', headline: 'Ready? Go!', sub: 'Beat the clock to win.' },
    guide: { signs: 'A studio of saturated purple and blue light with yellow and pink accents; big rounded cards with thick borders that slam in exactly on the beat; numbers that count (1, 2, 3, a score, a timer bar); flashes between rounds; a punchy final answer card; everything bounces with the music.', build: 'Use a music track with its beats (Audio, beats, or the kit beats tool) and start every entrance on a beat. Cards are rounded rects (radius 2-3) in the accent colours with a thick white stroke and the text on top, entering with text-slam or pop and an impact sound. A big number for each tip (text-count or odometer), a timer bar that grows (grow, origin start) and tr-flash between rounds. Keep a pulse (scale 1.04-1.08) on the current card in time with the beat. End on one big answer card with a success sound.' },
