    guide: { signs: 'A dark green (or black) board with a faint smudge of old chalk; everything in soft, slightly broken white chalk lines, with yellow and pink chalk for what matters; handwritten sums, labels and diagrams written out step by step; circled answers and underlines; things are erased with a soft fade, not wiped hard.', build: 'Text in the chalk fonts, written on with wipe from left at the voice\'s pace; diagrams as path layers (stroke 0.3-0.45, the chalk colours) drawn with draw, and shapes as outlines with a "sketch" clip (style hachure or none, roughness 1.5-2, the chalk colour) for a broken chalk edge. A boil (amount 1, fps 6) keeps the chalk alive. Circle the answer with a drawn ellipse path in yellow. Erase between parts with a fade that blurs out. Pin each step to the word that names it.' },
