    guide: { signs: 'Warm rice paper and black ink only, in washes from deep black to the palest grey; a few confident brush strokes (bamboo, a mountain, a branch, a circle), lots of empty paper; one small red square seal; calm, slow pacing with long holds; type small and quiet beside the painting.', build: 'Paint shapes and pictures on with the brush reveal (1-3 strokes, 1.4-2 s); grey washes are shapes with soft edges (blur 0.3-0.6) at low opacity, layered from pale to dark; a single ensō circle is a path drawn with draw (stroke 1.2+, round caps). A small red rect with a thin inner border is the seal, placed last with a soft pop. Keep at least half the frame empty. Text fades in with a little blur. No hard cuts: fade through the paper.' },
